      <activity id="00f883fe-649b-5f33-85eb-cc5c2604a2db" activityNameId="1f102a3d-017a-54d5-8b5e-cdd64b1a260e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Methane, from biological methanation, with carbon from municipal waste incineration plant, with heat recove [74920732a0]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Methane, from biological methanation, with carbon from municipal waste incineration plant, with heat recovery (100:0 alloc.)
Based on stoichiometry, for every kilogram of methane produced, the system would consume approximately 2.75 kilograms of CO2 and 0.5 kilograms of H2, and produce approximately 2.25 kilograms of water. Rest of info Adapted from BioCat II project Annex I 2014. Consider 51.3 kg CH4 per full-load hour. Reactor heat re-circulated at the wastewater treatment plant, hence not considered here. Infrastructure missing. Note that a 100:0 CO2 alloc. is applied: the carbon dioxide emissions from the MSWI plant are entirely allocated to the cement plant, but the carbon capture efforst fall within the synthetic natural gas producer's system boundaries. The combustion of the resulting synthetic natural gas does not lead to any carbon dioxide emissions. Source: https://energiforskning.dk/sites/energiforskning.dk/files/slutrapporter/12164_annex_1_p2g_biocat_lca_final_report.pdf

 UUID: fb92538e-6c1c-37b6-be71-a7ddc1165ccb
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fb92538e-6c1c-37b6-be71-a7ddc1165ccb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
